// THE UNDERTAKER'S OUTFIT (Corey, 2026-12 October 2026) - five pieces, bought with Death tokens,
// worth nothing to anybody but the person wearing them.
//
// THE SHOP SELLS STATUS, NOT POWER. Corey's rule, 12 October: nothing that changes a combat number,
// nothing that can be used against another player. So every piece below carries NO param= bonuses
// at all - not zeroes, nothing - and `category` names them as clothing rather than armour. A piece
// that one day wants a stat has to be argued for, not typed in.
//
// THE MESHES ARE THE NPC'S OWN, repainted by tools/models/gendeathtoken.py: the same black the
// Undertaker wears, with the same gold band on the hat. Three meshes per piece, because a worn item
// needs all three - the item's own mesh for the pack slot and the floor, a *_manwear and a
// *_womanwear - and the generator tints each one at the SAME light scale, or the same hat would be
// two different blacks depending on who put it on.
//
// THE CAMERAS ARE THE SOURCE ITEMS' OWN, unchanged. A repaint is the same mesh, so it cannot need a
// different camera from the thing it repaints; copying them is not laziness, it is the only answer
// that can be right. (The source items' recol1s/recol1d lines are NOT copied: those map a source
// colour that the repaint no longer contains, so they would be a no-op pretending to be a decision.)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHY EVERY PIECE CARRIES destroy_death AND pvp_token_bounty
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Corey asked what you get for killing someone wearing this in the Wilderness. The answer, before
// this file existed, was NOTHING: BOTH_DROPSLOT in the engine sends tradeables to the killer and
// untradeables back to the victim, so the hat landed at the dead player's feet flagged to them and
// they walked back for it. A cosmetic that cannot be lost is a taunt with no stake behind it, and
// with no Wilderness Slayer master this shop is the whole of the wilderness identity.
//
// So: die in the Wilderness wearing a piece and it is DESTROYED, and whoever killed you is paid a
// quarter of its price in Death tokens (player/scripts/death.rs2).
//
// DESTROYED RATHER THAN DROPPED, and this is the part that matters. Corey: "if we allow them to
// pick it up again, that could bring in boosting... someone has the item, gets killed by their
// friend for 50 tokens, then picks it up and they kill them again, over and over." It does not even
// need a friend; an alt does it alone. Dropping the piece back makes the cycle free, and a free
// cycle that pays 50 tokens is a token printer with a kill animation. Destroying it makes one cycle
// cost 200 and pay 50 - the pair burns 150 tokens a turn.
//
//   THE INVARIANT: pvp_token_bounty MUST BE STRICTLY LESS THAN cost.
//   Tokens are untradeable, so paying a killer is the ONLY route from one account to another. At a
//   quarter that route loses three tokens for every one it moves. At or above the price it prints.
//   tools/slayer_battery.py fails on bounty >= cost, so this cannot be typed wrong quietly.
//
// destroy_death DOES NOT DESTROY ANYTHING - the name is aspirational. It is read in three places and
// all three mean "not eligible to be one of the items you keep". It is here so a piece can never be
// one of the three an unskulled player keeps and PROTECT ITEM CAN NEVER SAVE ONE: without it the
// stake is conditional, and conditional is where the next exploit lives. It also makes the Items
// Kept on Death screen tell the truth. The actual destroying is death.rs2's job.
//
// cost IS THE TOKEN PRICE. One shop, one multiplier (~calc_shop_value ends in scale($mult, 1000,
// $cost)), so an item's gp cost IS what it costs in tokens at the Undertaker's 1000 per mille. The
// same pattern Grace's graceful pieces use.

[undertaker_hat]
name=Undertaker's hat
desc=Tall, black, and a band of gold for the one who is paying.
model=obj_undertaker_hat
manwear=npc_undertaker_hat,0
womanwear=obj_undertaker_hat_womanwear,0
manhead=npc_undertaker_hat_head
womanhead=obj_undertaker_hat_womanhead
wearpos=hat
2dzoom=800
2dxan=152
2dyan=156
2dxof=5
2dyof=-10
weight=453g
cost=200
iop2=Wear
tradeable=no
category=clothing_hat
param=destroy_death,^true
param=pvp_token_bounty,50

[undertaker_coat]
name=Undertaker's coat
desc=Cut for standing still in, at the edge of a crowd.
model=obj_undertaker_coat
manwear=npc_undertaker_coat,0
manwear2=npc_undertaker_coat2
womanwear=obj_undertaker_coat_womanwear,0
womanwear2=obj_undertaker_coat_womanwear2
wearpos=torso
wearpos2=arms
2dzoom=1373
2dxan=452
2dxof=-1
2dyof=7
weight=1000g
cost=200
iop2=Wear
tradeable=no
category=clothing_torso
param=destroy_death,^true
param=pvp_token_bounty,50

[undertaker_trousers]
